   "notes": [
    "Actual results for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2023, as the town reported them to the Census Bureau's Annual Survey of State and Local Government Finances. Not a budget.",
    "The Census surveys every government only in Census of Governments years (2022) and a sample in other years, so FY 2023 is the latest available.",
    "Public schools are run by county boards of education, which are separate governments, so they are not included. Residents also pay Morgan County.",
    "Covers every fund, including water, sewer, electric and other utilities. Debt service counts interest and principal repaid; borrowing and transfers between funds are left out.",
    "Debt service leaves out $69,000 of principal repaid with new borrowing the town did not spend on capital that year, most likely refinancing or a rolled-over note.",
    "Courts, legal services, public buildings, housing and community development count as overhead.",
    "Debt is long-term debt outstanding plus short-term debt at year end.",
    "Political money is not scored: contributions to West Virginia city candidates were not loaded.",
    "Transparency practices have not been checked yet, so they are not scored."
